{
  "id": "instrumental-conditioning",
  "term": "instrumental conditioning",
  "definition": "Instrumental conditioning is a form of learning in which behaviour is shaped through performing a task, initially in a goal-directed way but, with repeated practice, often becoming more automatic and habit-like. In this process, behaviour can become less flexible and less sensitive to changes in the value of the outcome.",
